Origin and modifications
------------------------

Substrate began as a fork of the Jina AI Reader project
(https://github.com/jina-ai/reader), by way of Harsh Gupta's Docker-deployable
adaptation (https://github.com/hargup/reader).

As required by section 4(b) of the Apache License, the significant changes made
in this derivative work are:

  * Firebase and Google Cloud Functions were removed entirely; the project is
    now a plain Docker Compose stack with no cloud dependency.
  * The single application was split into an API and independent services. The
    browser, the segmenter and the model servers each run in their own
    container, and the API orchestrates them over HTTP.
  * The backend was rewritten on NestJS with Prisma; the crawl cache moved from
    a mock Firestore to Postgres, and is optional.
  * Capabilities were added that the original did not have: web search over
    self-hosted SearXNG, a segmenter with six chunking strategies, embeddings
    and reranking served by local open-weight models, image downloading, and a
    browser console.
  * The image alt-text captioning feature of the original was removed.
  * Security handling was reworked, including SSRF protection covering IPv6 and
    redirect chains, and content-type validation of stored files.

